+++ b/docs/querying/functions.md
@@ -816,8 +816,28 @@ label values are equal, elements are sorted by their full label sets.
 Please note that `sort_by_label` only affects the results of instant queries, as
 range query results always have a fixed output ordering.

-`sort_by_label` uses [natural sort
-order](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_sort_order).
+Label values are classified independently and sorted in this order:
+
+1. Values starting with whitespace, ordered by their original strings using
+   [natural sort order](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_sort_order).
+2. Positive infinity.
+3. Finite numbers.
+4. Negative infinity.
+5. Durations, by magnitude (units `ns`, `us`, `µs`, `μs`, `ms`, `s`, `m`, `h`, `d`, `w`, `y`).
+6. Byte sizes, by magnitude (SI units such as `kB` or `MB`, and IEC units such as `KiB` or `MiB`).
+7. Semantic versions, with an optional `v` prefix.
+8. IP addresses, with IPv4 before IPv6.
+9. CIDR prefixes, by network address, then prefix length (shorter first).
+10. RFC 3339 timestamps, by instant.
+11. Other strings, using natural sort order.
+
+Numbers, durations, and byte sizes accept signed decimal coefficients and
+scientific notation, and their magnitudes are compared without rounding.
+Semantic versions require all three core components. IPv4-mapped IPv6 addresses
+remain IPv6. Empty values, NaN literals, and invalid typed forms use natural
+string ordering. Values starting with whitespace are never parsed as typed
+values. When typed values compare equal, their original strings break the tie
+using natural sort order.

 ## `sort_by_label_desc()`

